+      "kind": "lemma",
+      "title": "A bounded common Gaussian covariance mode changes centred extremal limits",
+      "statement": "Let Y_N(x)=X_N(x)+Z for a finite Gaussian field X_N and independent Z~N(0,sigma^2), sigma>0, shared by every site. All covariance entries change by sigma^2. For any deterministic centring m_N, max Y_N-m_N=max X_N-m_N+Z, and if the latter X maximum tends in law to a real M, the Y maximum tends to M+Z, a different law. Heights and level-set thresholds translate exactly by Z. Thus a uniformly bounded covariance difference alone cannot force identical extremal limit laws. This changes the off-diagonal finite covariance limit and need not meet a specified continuum Green-function hypothesis.",
+      "proof_text": "# C0008: an exact common-Gaussian-mode check on covariance comparisons\n\nLabel: proof of a limitation of bounded covariance perturbations, pending w347 KEEP. No disproof of Problem 16.8 or full universality result is claimed.\n\nFor any finite centred Gaussian field X_N and an independent Z~N(0,sigma^2) with sigma>0, let Y_N(x)=X_N(x)+Z at every site. Then Cov(Y_N(x),Y_N(y))-Cov(X_N(x),X_N(y))=sigma^2 uniformly. For any deterministic centring m_N, max Y_N-m_N=max X_N-m_N+Z exactly. If max X_N-m_N converges in law to M, independence gives max Y_N-m_N -> M+Z. The laws of M and M+Z differ: equality would imply phi_M(t)=phi_M(t) exp(-sigma^2 t^2/2); continuity and phi_M(0)=1 make this impossible at sufficiently small nonzero t.\n\nThe full point measure of heights is translated by Z, and the number of sites above a threshold t for Y is the number above t-Z for X. A bounded covariance difference therefore cannot alone force identical centred-maximum, extremal-process, or level-set limit laws. A universality claim must specify any allowed model-dependent smooth mode, centring, constant, intensity or decoration law.\n\nThis example changes the off-diagonal O(1) covariance limit. It may fail the exact continuum Green-function hypothesis in the source and is expressly not a counterexample to that complete hypothesis package. The prior conditional interpolation route needs its own theorem with the correct limit identification; an O(1) comparison by itself only provides comparisons, not equality of laws.\n\nSource: C0008-A001 and the exact question in the 2026-09-07 intake, citing Biskup, Problem 16.8, p.222. The intake records the centred-maximum result of Ding-Roy-Zeitouni (Ann. Probab. 2017) but leaves the full level-set/extremal-process generality unverified.\n\nExact reference for the already-known centred-maximum part, checked in the cached Biskup bibliography, item 59: J. Ding, R. Roy and O. Zeitouni (2017), Convergence of the centered maximum of log-correlated Gaussian fields, Ann. Probab. 45(6A), 3886-3928. This is a maximum theorem, not a verified answer to the full level-set/extremal-process question.\n",
